In the situation of [[def-graded-specht-module-by-homogeneous-standard-tableaux]], define d^A(lambda) for an ADDABLE i-node A to be the number of addable i-nodes strictly ABOVE A minus the number of removable i-nodes strictly ABOVE A. Define the codegree of a standard tableau $T$ by $\operatorname{codeg}(\varnothing):=0$ and $\operatorname{codeg}(T):=d^A(\mu^A)+\operatorname{codeg}(T_{\le d-1})$, where $A$ is the node containing $d$ and $\mu^A=\mu\setminus A$. Define the defect of a residue content $\alpha\in Q_+$ by $\operatorname{def}(\alpha):=(\Lambda_0,\alpha)-(\alpha,\alpha)/2$ (the symmetric form of [[def-cyclic-affine-type-a-cartan-datum]]). Then for every partition $\mu$ with content $\alpha$ and every standard $\mu$-tableau $T$:

1. $d_A(\mu)+d^A(\mu^A)=d_i(\mu)+1$ where $i$ is the residue of the removable node $A$ and $d_i(\mu)=\#\{\text{addable }i\text{-nodes of }\mu\}-\#\{\text{removable }i\text{-nodes of }\mu\}$;
2. $d_i(\mu)=(\Lambda_0-\alpha,\alpha_i)$;
3. $\operatorname{def}(\alpha)=\operatorname{def}(\alpha-\alpha_i)+d_i(\mu)+1$;
4. $\deg(T)+\operatorname{codeg}(T)=\operatorname{def}(\alpha)$;
5. removing a brick does not change the codegree: if $m\to_T m+1\to_T\cdots\to_T d$ and $S=T_{\le m-1}$, then $\operatorname{codeg}(S)=\operatorname{codeg}(T)$ whenever (i) $m,\dots,d$ occupy nodes in the first row of the first component of $T$, or (ii) $d-m+1=e$ (the quantum characteristic).

No choice is used.
